{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789863588,"nonce":"hbfkehsqYJgtw0SDOwOPAVDq4aE=","title":"The trusted variant of a function that assigns None to an instance parameter dereferences null","message":"The trusted variant takes every instance-typed parameter to be an instance for the whole body; a body that assigns the parameter (`for i in range(3): try: out.append(t.v) except AttributeError: ...; t = None`) reads through null on the next pass and dies with SIGSEGV instead of raising AttributeError. `self` had the same assumption.\n\nA parameter the body assigns, or shares with a nested body through a cell, is not trusted; its reads are checked like any variable's.","files":null}]}